    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="38.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 38.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="38.2" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="72" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif ðises<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_38-2.lnote.oe.5"/> hwæt beforan cyninges ealdormonnes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_38-2.lnote.oe.6"/> gingran gelimpe oððe cyninges preoste<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_38-2.lnote.oe.7"/>, XXX scill. to wite.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_38-2.lnote.oe.4"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="38.2" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="72" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif ðyses hwæt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_38-2.lnote.oe.1"/> beforan cyninges ealdermonnes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_38-2.lnote.oe.2"/> gingran<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_38-2.lnote.oe.3"/> gelimpe oððe cyninges preoste<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_38-2.lnote.oe.4-2"/>, XXX scillingas to wite.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="38.2" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="72" ed="#liebermann"/>Eft. Gyf ðisses hwæt beforan cyninges ealdormannes gingran gelimpe oððe cyninges preoste, ðrittig scill. to wíte.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="38.2" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="73" ed="#liebermann"/>Si horum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_38-2.lnote.oe.6-2"/> aliquid coram regis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_38-2.lnote.oe.7-2"/> aldremanno<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_38-2.lnote.oe.8"/> iuniore<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Af_38-2.lnote.oe.9"/> contigerit aut coram presbitero regis, sit wita XXX sol.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="80" ed="#attenborough"/>Gif<ptr type="editorNote" n="23" target="#Af_38-2.attnote.fn.23"/> ðises hwæt beforan cyninges ealdormonnes gingran gelimpe oððe cyninges preoste, XXX scill. to wite.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="39.2" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="338" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Gif ðises hwæt beforan cyninges ealdormonnes gingran gelimpe oððe cyninges preoste, XXX scill to wite.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_38-2.lnote.de.1"/><pb n="73" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn etwas derart<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_38-2.lnote.de.2"/> vor dem Vertreter des königlichen Ealdorman<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_38-2.lnote.de.3"/> oder einem Königskleriker<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_38-2.lnote.de.4"/> vorkommt: 30<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_38-2.lnote.de.5"/> Schill. als Strafgeld.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If anything of this kind happens before the deputy of the king’s ealdorman or a king’s priest: 30 shillings as a fine.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="81" ed="#attenborough"/>If anything of this kind takes place in the presence of an official subordinate<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Af_38-2.attnote.n.1"/> to an <hi rend="italic">ealdorman</hi> of the king, [or in the presence of] a king's priest, he shall pay a fine of 30 shillings.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="415" ed="#whitelock"/>If any of this takes place in the presence of the deputy of the king’s ealdorman, or of the king’s priest, 30 shillings [is to be paid] as a fine.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="339" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If something of this nature should occur before the subordinate of a king’s ealdorman or the king’s priest, 30 shillings as fine.</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_38-2.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðisses <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðisses Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_38-2.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-man. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-man. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_38-2.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-st ðrittig <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-st ðrittig Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_38-2.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="spaced">gesylle</hi> <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">gesylle</hi> added by Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_38-2.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">æt <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">æt on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_38-2.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">zweites</hi> e <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur;</hi> o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">second e on an erasure; o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_38-2.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">hinter</hi> i <hi rend="italic">ein Buchst. radirt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">a letter erased after i</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_38-2.lnote.oe.4-2" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">erstes</hi> e <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">first e on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_38-2.lnote.oe.6-2" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">73</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">a. h. <hi rend="italic">Hk;</hi> h. a. <hi rend="italic">fehlt Brti</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">a. h. Hk; h. a. lacking in Brti</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_38-2.lnote.oe.7-2" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">73</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">r. a. <hi rend="italic">fehlt Brti</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">r. a. lacking in Brti</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_38-2.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">73</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">CXX sol. w., i. for. <hi rend="italic">wiederholt irrig Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">CXX sol. w., i. for. repeated in error by Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_38-2.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">73</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">inueniri <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">inueniri Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_38-2.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Ferner’ Rb B</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘Further’ Rb B</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_38-2.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Fechten oder Waffenzücken im Gericht</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Fighting or drawing weapons in court</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_38-2.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">59</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Ealdorman 20c. 21; ‘jüngerem Ealdorman’ Q falsch; vielleicht las er urspr. <hi rend="italic">-manni,</hi> denn <hi rend="italic">iunior</hi> (<hi rend="italic">s. Wb</hi>) sagt er auch sonst für ‘Unterbeamter’, wie andere ebenfalls: Bi 149. — ‘Sheriff’ missverstehen Inst. (? <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 1g), Kemble (<hi rend="italic">Saxons</hi> II 139), Schmid 597b. Allein zu solcher Auslegung wäre Verbindung von <hi rend="italic">cyninges</hi> (‘öffentlich, staatlich’) nicht (wie Af 38 und Schmid auch hier) mit dem ersten, sondern dem zweiten Worte nötig. Dafür fehlt Beleg. Wenn Af hier den Königsvogt meinte, erhellt kein Grund, dass er ihn anders als in 22. 34 nannte. Und andere <hi rend="italic">gingran</hi> des Ealdorman (<hi rend="italic">s. Gl</hi> 20c) sind zweifellos keine Königsvögte. Der Königsvogt ward vielleicht von Af hier nicht genannt, weil er selbstverständlich im Empfang der Busse für Bruch seines Gerichtsfriedens (<hi rend="italic">s. Gl</hi> 4) gleich rangierte entweder mit dem Ealdorman oder mit dem Königskaplan. Ein Priester als Sheriff (<hi rend="italic">s. Gl</hi> 7) kommt vor</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Ealdorman 20c. 21; ‘junior ealdorman’ Q, wrongly; perhaps he originally read <hi rend="italic">-manni,</hi> for he uses <hi rend="italic">iunior</hi> (<hi rend="italic">see Wb</hi>) elsewhere too for ‘subordinate official’, as others also do: Bi 149. — Inst. (? <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 1g), Kemble (<hi rend="italic">Saxons</hi> II 139) and Schmid 597b misunderstand it as ‘sheriff’. But such an interpretation would require <hi rend="italic">cyninges</hi> (‘public, of the state’) to be connected not with the first word (as in Af 38, and as Schmid takes it here too) but with the second. There is no evidence for this. If Af meant the king’s reeve here, there is no apparent reason why he should have named him differently from 22. 34. And other <hi rend="italic">gingran</hi> of the ealdorman (see <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 20c) are undoubtedly not king’s reeves. The king’s reeve was perhaps not named here by Af because, in receiving the compensation for breach of the peace of his court (see <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 4), he naturally ranked equal either with the ealdorman or with the king’s chaplain. A priest as sheriff (see <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 7) does occur</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_38-2.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">59</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nicht ‘Vertreter des Bischofs [des späteren Shire-Mitvorsitzenden]’. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Königskleriker 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Not ‘deputy of the bishop [the later co-president of the shire court]’. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Königskleriker 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_38-2.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">59</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Inst. meinen wohl nicht (wie Schmid denkt) Normannische Schilling, sondern übernehmen die Zahl nur mechanisch</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Inst. probably do not mean Norman shillings (as Schmid thinks), but merely take over the number mechanically</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_38-2.attnote.fn.23" n="23" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">80</biblScope></bibl><label>Gif</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">Eft. Gyf</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Af_38-2.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">198</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Schmid and Kemble understand <hi rend="italic">gingran</hi> to mean sheriff; but there is no evidence that such an official was in existence at this time.</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
